From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:10:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] view: An app started on the phone is maximized with a second
 screen too

phoc_view_want_auto_maximize() looks at the view's output during the first
commit, when the view is still at the layout's origin. With a second screen
the phone isn't there: the layout now has the virtual screen left of the
phone. So the window floated, centered on the phone, instead of filling it.
The placement on map knows the screen and maximizes it there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/view.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/view.c b/src/view.c
index a7a762b..fa236b8 100644
--- a/src/view.c
+++ b/src/view.c
@@ -1818,6 +1818,15 @@ view_place_initially (PhocView *self)
     return;
   }
 
+  /* On the phone it is maximized. The auto-maximize of the first commit can't tell: the view is
+   * still at the layout's origin then, and that is not the phone's place with a second screen */
+  if (target && !self->parent && view_output_is_phone (target) &&
+      !phoc_view_is_fullscreen (self) && !phoc_desktop_get_auto_maximize (desktop) &&
+      PHOC_VIEW_GET_CLASS (self)->want_auto_maximize (self)) {
+    phoc_view_maximize (self, target);
+    return;
+  }
+
   if (phoc_view_is_floating (self)) {
     view_center (self, target);
     return;
